  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Slavia Ukraina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the project is improve vulnerable children&#x2019;s life and is focused on three outcomes: 1) Supporting vulnerable families through the provision of food aid, 2) Protection of children&#x2019;s mental health through the provision of psycho-social support 3) Supporting vulnerable families through the provision of school supplies. In 6-month 2.500 vulnerable persons in 9 regions of Ukraine will be assisted in the 3 areas. As Ukraine is suffering from war many people are living as IDPs or under bad conditions and struggle to find necessities for their daily living. Children are affected by war trauma why we through counseling, training and camps will address these issues in order to make them deal with loss and insecurity. Local churches are the center for the activities; distributing items or organizing camps and activities for children. Food support and Psycho-social support is given to 9 frontline regions while the school support is given to IDPs living in Lviv area.</narrative>
  </description>
